==Battleground==
===<u>Chapter 1</u>===
{{EnemiesAppearing|Pigge|Elizabeth the LVIth}}
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~36.67 seconds<sup>500f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*10 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.

===<u>Chapter 2</u>===
{{EnemiesAppearing|St. Pigge the 2nd|Elizabeth the LVIth}}
*2 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn, delay 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*4 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.

===<u>Chapter 3</u>===
{{EnemiesAppearing|Pigge|Elizabeth the LVIth|Bore}}
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~36.67 seconds<sup>500f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can solo this stage if you bring an Attack UP [[Cat Combo]] such as [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]]. Simply spawn him once you have enough money and watch him eventually beat the stage on his own. If you own [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], this stage becomes trivial, as its wave blocker effectively makes the main gimmick of this stage redundant. If you own a level 30+ [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], you could effectively clear the stage just with it and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]]/Octopus.

For Chapter 3, you may want to bring in a unit like [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] or [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] to effectively stall the Bore and perhaps even [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to block Elizabeth the LVIth's [[Wave Attack|waves]].

